Reject chartr() output that cannot be represented in the native locale.

When a UTF-8 translation spec maps an ASCII input character to a code
point unavailable in the native locale, wcstombs() returns (size_t)-1.
do_chartr() cast this to -1, passed it to CallocCharBuf(), then called
markKnown() on the resulting unterminated allocation.  mkCharCE() reads
past the heap buffer while computing its length.  Keep the size_t result
and reject conversion failure before allocating.

A smaller reproducer is LC_ALL=C Rscript -e
    'chartr("a", intToUtf8(256L), "a")'

The upstream PR also adds a regression test (tests/reg-tests-1a.R), not
carried here.

Found by OSS-Fuzz: testcase 5327307326423040 (afl_r_character,
Heap-buffer-overflow READ 3).

Upstream status: r-devel/r-svn PR #383, filed 2026-10-16.
Delete this patch once the fix lands in R trunk.

--- a/src/main/character.c
+++ b/src/main/character.c
@@ -1630,9 +1630,13 @@ attribute_hidden SEXP do_chartr(SEXP call, SEXP op, SEXP args, SEXP env)
 		    wcstoutf8(cbuf, wc, nb);
 		    SET_STRING_ELT(y, i, mkCharCE(cbuf, CE_UTF8));
 		} else {
-		    nb = (int) wcstombs(NULL, wc, 0);
-		    cbuf = CallocCharBuf(nb);
-		    wcstombs(cbuf, wc, nb + 1);
+		    size_t nbytes = wcstombs(NULL, wc, 0);
+		    if (nbytes == (size_t)-1)
+			error(_("translated string is not representable in the current locale"));
+		    if (nbytes > INT_MAX)
+			error(_("R character strings are limited to 2^31-1 bytes"));
+		    cbuf = CallocCharBuf(nbytes);
+		    wcstombs(cbuf, wc, nbytes + 1);
 		    SET_STRING_ELT(y, i, markKnown(cbuf, el));
 		}
 		R_Free(cbuf);
